<http://data.silknow.org/object/aab9388a-448a-3a0e-aa6c-2a14a703475e/observation/2>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Writing cabinet(called in Würzburg a <i>trisur)</i> of bureau form, with cupboard above, veneered in walnut and other woods, with turtle shell, horn, pewter, brass and ivory, the marquetry including the date, 1716 and the arms and cypher of Jacob Gallus von Hohlach (1665-1724). Made in Würzburg, 1716 by Jacob Arend of Koblenz and Johannes Wittalm of Vienna, working for Servatius Arend, the court cabinet-maker in Würzburg."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/aab9388a-448a-3a0e-aa6c-2a14a703475e> .

