<http://data.silknow.org/object/aab9388a-448a-3a0e-aa6c-2a14a703475e/observation/5>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/historical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Such writing cabints, of English form, became signifiers of the owner's status and education.  They often appeared in portraits to suggest the education and wisdom of those in authority. The main flap is high and not easily suited to writing but the two side flaps may have been used by secretaries, standing to take dictation."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/aab9388a-448a-3a0e-aa6c-2a14a703475e> .

