        rdfs:comment        "Peter Thornton, 'A Cabinet for a Würzburg Patron'. <i>Apollo</i> LXXXIX, No. 88 (1969), p. 448\nMax von Freeden, 'Ein fränkischer Prunkschrank in England'.   \nCope, Sophie. 'The Cabinet with the Letter: Luxury and Poverty in 18th-century Würzburg' in <i>V&amp;A Online Journa</i>l Issue No. 6, Summer 2014, ISSN 2043-667X, accessible at: \nhttp://www.vam.ac.uk/content/journals/research-journal/issue-no.-6-summer-2014/the-letter-in-the-writing-cabinet-the-emotional-life-of-an-18th-century-journeyman\nSeyler, Katrin, 'The Letter in the Writing Cabinet: The Emotional Life of an 18th-century Journeyman', in <i>V&amp;A Online Journa</i>l Issue No. 6 Summer 2014, ISSN 2043-667X, accessible at:\nhttp://www.vam.ac.uk/content/journals/research-journal/issue-no.-6-summer-2014/the-letter-in-the-writing-cabinet-the-emotional-life-of-an-18th-century-journeyman\nElizabeth Miller and Hilary Young, eds., <i>The Arts of Living. Europe 1600-1815</i>. V&A Publishing, 2015. ISBN: 978 1 85177 807 2, illustrated p. 125."@en ;
